        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: The Brothers Creeggan, The dB's\n- People: Jim Creeggan, Andy Creeggan, Ian McLauchlan, Peter Holsapple, Chris Stamey, Will Rigby, Gene Holder\n- Genres: alternative rock, jazz, power pop, jangle pop\n- Places: Canada, America\n\nFacts:\n- The dB's first came into prominence in the late 1970s and 1980s as an American power pop and jangle pop group.\n- The dB's band members are Peter Holsapple, Chris Stamey, Will Rigby, and Gene Holder.\n- The Brothers Creeggan is a Canadian alternative rock and jazz band.\n- The Brothers Creeggan is composed of Jim Creeggan, Andy Creeggan, and Ian McLauchlan.\n- Jim Creeggan plays upright bass, guitar, bass guitar, and provides vocals in The Brothers Creeggan.\n- Andy Creeggan plays guitar, piano, accordion, percussion, and provides vocals in The Brothers Creeggan.\n- Ian McLauchlan plays drums in The Brothers Creeggan.",
